course: dictionary
lesson: 15691
title: One word, several meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning, and tipped is a good example. You find out which meaning it has by reading the words around it. «She tipped the water out of the jug.» The words water and out are the clues: tipped means turned over so the water poured out.
explain: «The family tipped the waiter because the meal was great.» The clue is the waiter. After a meal, people can give a tip, a little extra money, to thank someone for their service. Here tipped means gave that extra money.
explain: «The horse was tipped to win the race.» Tipped to win means people expected it to win. «The pen had a felt-tipped end.» Here tipped describes the end of the pen. Always ask which meaning fits, then put your meaning into the sentence and check that it makes sense.
fact: Tipped can mean turned over or tilted so that something fell or poured.
fact: Tipped can mean gave a small extra amount of money to someone for their service, like a waiter.
fact: Tipped to win means expected or predicted to win.
fact: Tipped can describe something with a tip or end of a certain kind, as in «felt-tipped pens».
fact: Tipped someone off means secretly warned them or told them something.
exercise: «She tipped the water out of the jug.» What does tipped mean here? | *Turned over so the water poured out | Stood still in the sun | Wrote on the jug with a pen | Filled up with cold water
exercise: «The runner was tipped to win the race.» What does tipped to win mean? | *Was expected to win | Was given a prize before the race | Was tipped over by the wind | Was too tired to run
exercise: «The children drew a flower with a felt-tipped pen.» What does felt-tipped describe? | A pen that was lost in the rain | A pen that was spilled on the floor | *A pen with a tip made of felt | A pen that was given away as a tip
test: «We tipped the waiter two dollars because the meal was great.» What does tipped mean? | *Gave a small extra amount of money for good service | Spilled on the table | Cut into small pieces | Pointed to the menu
test: «Our friend tipped us off about the surprise party.» What does tipped off mean? | Gave us a prize | Tilted us towards the door | Told us to be quiet | *Secretly warned us or told us something
exam: «The cup tipped over in the wind, so the tea spilled everywhere.» What does tipped mean? | Had a gold tip on its handle | Was tipped to win a prize | *Turned over and fell | Gave money to the cup
